    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0487" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Council of Foreign Ministers Files: Lot M–88: CFM
                    London Minutes</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Record of Decisions of the Twenty-Ninth Meeting of the
                        Council of Foreign Ministers, Lancaster House, London, September 30, 1945, 3
                        p.m.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>London</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1945-09-30T15:00:00+00:00">September 30, 1945, 3 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">C.F.M.(P) (45) 29th Meeting</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Present</hi>
                </p>
                <table rend="width: 98%" rendition="#center">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell rend="padding-left: 4em">U.K.</cell>
                        <cell rend="padding-left: 4em">U.S.A</cell>
                        <cell rend="padding-left: 4em">U.S.S.R</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Mr. Bevin</cell>
                        <cell>Mr. Byrnes (Chairman)</cell>
                        <cell>M. Molotov</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Sir R. I. Campbell</cell>
                        <cell>Mr. J. Dunn</cell>
                        <cell>M. F. T. Gousev</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Sir A. Clark Kerr</cell>
                        <cell>Mr. B. V. Cohen</cell>
                        <cell>M. K. V. Novikov</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Mr. A. Duff Cooper</cell>
                        <cell>Mr. J. F. Dulles</cell>
                        <cell>M. S. A. Golunski</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Mr. C. E. Bohlen</cell>
                        <cell>M. V. N. Pavlov</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <table rend="width: 80%" rendition="#center">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell rend="padding-left: 4em">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">France</hi>
                        </cell>
                        <cell rend="padding-left: 4em">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">China</hi>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>M. Bidault</cell>
                        <cell>Dr. Wang Shih Chieh</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>M. Couve de Murville</cell>
                        <cell>Dr. Wellington Koo</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>General Catroux</cell>
                        <cell>Dr. Victor Hoo</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>M. Alphand</cell>
                        <cell>Dr. Hollington Tong</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Mr. Yang Yun Chu</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <pb facs="0488" n="476" xml:id="pg476"/>
                <p rendition="#center">1. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austria: Ration Scales</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Council invited the Governments of the United Kingdom, United States,
                    U.S.S.R. and France to despatch telegrams to their representatives on the Allied
                    Council for Austria in the terms of the draft set out in C.F.M.(45) 82.<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d170-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">2. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Restitution</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Council invited the Deputies to continue their consideration of the question
                    of Restitution on the basis of the French memorandum (C.F.M.(45) 38<anchor
                        n="18" xml:id="d170-f2"/>).</p>
                <p rendition="#center">3. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preparation of Final
                        Protocol</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Council instructed the Protocol Committee to prepare drafts of four Protocols
                    on the lines proposed by M. Molotov, taking as a basis the Russian text prepared
                    by the Soviet Delegation.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">4. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preparation of Final
                        Communiqué</hi>
                </p>
                <p>An exchange of views took place. The Council agreed to meet again at 9:30 p.m.
                    that evening in order to consider (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) questions
                    arising on the final Protocol and Communiqué, and (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) the proposal of the Soviet Delegation regarding the future
                    procedure for the preparation of Peace Treaties.</p>
            </div>
